# Independent spec21 block projection authoring review

PASS, no blocking content discrepancy. Reviewed a163764e93e2809f8013d7bbe16721082f979143 to 652d3b2476416a1ead7332f12055d1a18018cfb6. The final manuscript SHA is b6a0fe957adc6abeae3c3791e4f0fa7822a5184bdc08ba2e4cdf3eeaaf70ed1f. Actual complete source and draft diffs were directly read, with authoring and AGENTS guidance; the author's marker checks were not treated as independent proof. Source before/after, manuscript before/after and both diffs are frozen here. The author manifest and all its declared payload bytes/hash are separately verified.

The complete Article structurally parses against current formal forms. An independent literal-base extractor verifies all 23 added/changed literal statements occur exactly in the canonical Markdown after its source line wrapping is removed. Three old lines are replaced and all unrelated lines retain exact bytes. This is structural checking, not production parse/lower. The renderer's explicit code sentence and the new explicit External Link sentence were read directly: /1 changes to /2, URL https://github.github.com/gfm/#tables-extension- and label GFMの表 are exact. Existing code/link values elsewhere are unchanged.

All new requirements survive: version upgrade without changing inherited display rules; matching registry/metadata and regeneration; no advertising old renderer capability; Body block ordering and unchanged RawCode constraints. Lists retain nonempty ordered/unordered, exactly one Paragraph/item, normal annotated Sentence concatenation, checked/unchecked/unspecified distinction, rejection of empty/multi-paragraph/nested/nonparagraph shapes, 0..999999999, same marker value rather than increment, Markdown numbering, marker-width Break indentation, rejection of adjacent independent lists and escaping checkbox-like Text.

Tables retain nonempty columns and explicit header, no promoted/invented header, permitted header-only form, row/cell order/count and four alignments, empty Sentence-cell exception without permitting empty headings/paragraphs/code, shared annotation/style/link/code processing, pipe escape with exactly one added escape consumed by GFM, retained backslash/backtick content, and rejection of Break/outer Text whitespace/multiblock without silent removal. The independent-parser validation requirement remains. Parallel/image/reference/inline Anchor remain unsupported; Relative/Page/assets/foreign remain NeedsResolution without ambient search or dummy registration, with no shrinking of Doc/HTML capability.

Paragraph boundaries match the Markdown: inherited Body and List explanation share one paragraph; Table and remaining unsupported features have separate paragraphs. Existing Section nesting and all prior full-page structure are unchanged. Ordinary statements use individual sentence literals, while inline code/link use explicit Sentence construction. The 128 added literal Ruby occurrences and changed prefix readings were read for Kanji-only bases and context: 非空, 開始値, 継続行, 昇格, 黙殺, 外端 etc. Kana and symbols remain outside Ruby (引き継ぐ, 委ねる, 区切り, 0〜999999999). No new translation is present and no gratuitous Anno/parallel is required.

No production implementation, manuscript or author evidence was edited. This is only independent review of the authored synchronization delta, not a full re-review of historical spec21, GFM behavior, runtime/browser execution or acceptance. Existing full-manuscript resource stops are not treated as content failures or successful execution. During the first scratch check root committed the dirty diff; an assertion expecting three changed lines against HEAD therefore stopped. The checker was bound to the original fixed a163764 base and succeeded; the manuscript hash remained unchanged. No source expectation was weakened to hide a content change.
